<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Styled Webpage Example</title>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>

    <header>

        <h1 id="main-heading">Modern Web Design Basics</h1>
        <p>Demonstrating clean CSS architecture and styling principles.</p>
    </header>

    <main class="container">

        <section class="card">
            <h2>Understanding the Box Model</h2>
            <p>Every element on a web page is a rectangular box made up of margins, borders, padding, and the actual content. This card has a solid border, custom internal padding, and external spacing via margins.</p>
        </section>

        <div id="special-callout">
            <h3>Complementary Color Scheme</h3>
            <p>This section uses a <span class="highlight-text">vibrant orange</span> accent color which sits opposite to the <span class="highlight-text" style="color: #1a2530;">deep navy</span> primary palette on the color wheel, creating high contrast and visual interest.</p>
        </div>

        <section id="contact-section">
            <h3>Get in Touch</h3>
            <p>This layout is intentionally styled with modern typography, pleasant padding, and structured borders instead of relying on default browser styling.</p>
        </section>

    </main>
</body>
</html>
